From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 04:14:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] feat: the agent measures with the headset's tape
 (survey, check_slope, /agent/observe)

brain.md S1 / B1, "the Quartermaster uses the tape": "measure every cabinet door" makes the
headset run its real measure tool over every structure-layer object of that label, and the
headset reports its own numbers back. The server never measures or estimates a size.

- scene_digest.py: digest(site, scale) from scene/<site>/structure.r<rev>.json (cached by site +
  file): counts by label, size groups, per-object {id,label,group,w_mm,h_mm,center,normal}, the 5
  longest high near-horizontal edges (gutter candidates), gravity_residual_deg. Only counts and
  groups reach the LLM (one system-prompt line, ~75 tokens for the kitchen).
- survey.py: the /agent/observe body, greedy 10 mm size grouping, spoken summaries ("18 doors in
  8 sizes: 6 at 26 by 28, ... Two didn't lock onto corners; they're amber."), the gutter verdict
  (1/4 in per 10 ft; drains / won't drain / inconclusive from fall +- uncertainty), and template
  answers for widest/narrowest/tallest/shortest/largest/smallest.
- agent.py: fast paths for "measure/survey/size up every|all|each|the [upper|left|...] <label>"
  -> survey {label, where, measure, request_id}, gutter/sill/ledge + slope/drain/fall/pitch ->
  check_slope {target, request_id, edge_ids}, a bare "stop" -> stop_survey; LLM tools survey,
  check_slope and survey_query (offered only once a survey exists); both headset tools end the
  turn with their spoken acknowledgement. The context gains `site` and `scale`: with a known site
  the reply counts ("Surveying 18 doors."), "doors" means cabinet_door in a kitchen, a missing
  label or structure layer is answered straight instead of sending an empty sweep.
- app.py: POST /agent/observe (survey_result | slope_result) -> {reply, actions, job_id} with
  show_survey {request_id, label, groups, unverified, skipped, focus} or add_note; `tts: true`
  adds audio like /voice/command. System prompt: numbers only from tools or the notebook.
- api.md: the endpoint, four actions, two context fields, the fast-path phrasings.

Rebased onto integration/grok-all (c706f13), where F10 already owns `server/survey.py`,
`tests/test_survey.py`, the `survey_condition` tool, `_SURVEY_RE` and the `show_survey` action
`{survey_id, pins, label}`:
- our module is `server/tape_survey.py` and our tests `tests/test_tape_survey.py`; the matcher is
  `_TAPE_SURVEY_RE`, the session's stored report `Session.tape_survey` (F10 keeps `survey_id`);
- our card action is renamed `show_tape_survey` (same args), so one action name has one shape;
- "survey" priority (row 4 of the fast-path table): a bare "stop" / "cancel the survey" first,
  then `fix_pin`, then the tape when a structure-object noun is the thing surveyed and no
  condition word (condition / damage / cracks / rot / rust / leaks) is said, then F10's
  `survey_condition` (roof, gutter(s), facade, building, and anything else with "survey");
- `check_slope` moved after the Grok stateless matchers (report, quote, safety, rules, finish,
  coach, labels) and `survey_query` is a stateful row after the reimagine words (`_fast_route`);
- `survey` and `check_slope` join the single early-exit tuple; their lines (and a template
  `survey_query` answer) go first, in call order, then the model's text, as for the Grok tools;
- the LLM's `survey` tool says "sizes only" and points condition checks at `survey_condition`.
Tests: +23 routing cases for both phrasings, the unchanged F10 args, and both surveys end to end
on one site. docs/integration-grok-features.md's priority table lists the new phrases.

